  "description": "Service lines (plan data) on the track network: nodes a (512, 1536) to g (6656, 1536), a tile apart, joined by straight edges e1 a-b to e6 f-g, each 1024 long, dead ends at both ends. Alpha (1536, 512), Beta (3584, 512) and Gamma (5632, 512) each have a platform on the half tile of track either side of their node, b, d and f; Delta (5632, 2560) has one on e6 [512, 1024], touching Gamma's past f at 512; Far (7680, 3584) has none. createLine checks invalidName, invalidLineStops (fewer than two, or a station twice in a row), unknownStation, and gives the standard window 06:00-24:00, the standard performance and no trains. A line's journey drives its stops out and back, turning round at the far end, from a berth of each platform of its first stop, going forward and then back, keeping the shortest round trip (the first among equals): here the end of the first stop's platform past its node going east, 512 units on from the node, so a first leg is 512 shorter than from node to node. Each leg takes the least whole second the line's performance builds a running curve for over it (Stage W2c, ARCHITECTURE decision 40); the round trip adds 1 minute at each call between the ends, out and back, and 2 at each end, and a line plans with it rounded up to whole minutes. Main (Alpha, Beta, Gamma) with the standard performance (1.5 and 2.5 km/h a second, 1/a + 1/b = 0.06 s\u00b2 a unit): a first leg of 1536 units, sqrt(2 x 1536 x 0.06) = 13.6, so 14 s, and three of 2048, sqrt(2 x 2048 x 0.06) = 15.7, so 16 s each, 62 + 120 + 240 = 422 s, 8 minutes. setLinePerformance checks the line, then the performance (an acceleration of 0 is invalidTrainPerformance); with a crawl, { acceleration 250, braking 250, topSpeed 1 }, 2048 units take 4 + 111.2 + 4 s, so 120, and 1536 take 4 + 82.4 + 4 s, so 91: the round trip 811 s, 14 minutes. The most trains is the round trip / 2 (the 2-minute minimum headway), at least 1: 4, then 7. Trains in service at a level are the count set, capped by that: peak 10 runs 4, then 7; the headway is the round trip / trains, rounded up: 2, 3, 8, then 2 and 5; no trains, no headway. The service level is the service day's at that minute while the window is open: standard day low from 0, peak 420-600 and 960-1200, off-peak otherwise, low from 1260; closed outside the window (a window may close up to 1800, 06:00 the next morning). Far cannot be driven (no platform). Shared calls at Gamma and Delta, whose platforms touch: from the end of Gamma's platform past f (e6 forward 512, where Delta's begins) it runs 512 units to the end of Delta's in 8 s, turns round there and comes back 1024 to f, the end of Gamma's platform going back, in 12 s: 260 s, 5 minutes, 2 trains. Main from Alpha to Gamma at the crawl: 3584 units out, 4 + 197.6 + 4 s, so 206, and 4096 back, 4 + 226.4 + 4 s, so 235: 681 s, 12 minutes. Removing Beta's platform past d and then e4 (d-e), which a platform on it would keep (trackEdgeHasPlatform), cuts Main off.",
